{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ba5jrivyycx3cripl4plvmrupksm3567bhmogwq2awb3vwgprrvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library was\n`c_src/` is a single 969-line file: an **stb_ds**-derived container library (dynamic arrays, open-addressed hash maps with bucketed probing, string interning arena, SipHash-2-4/string hashing) plus the two test helpers at the bottom (`strkey`, `str_dups`). `include/lib.h` declares only `str_dups`, but the shared library exports 16 symbols — all of which are now implemented.\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n`nm -D` / `readelf --dyn-syms` on the C `.so` vs the Rust `.so` produce the **identical set of 16 GLOBAL FUNC exports**, in both directions (nothing missing, nothing extra):\n`stbds_arrgrowf, stbds_arrfreef, stbds_rand_seed, stbds_hash_string, stbds_hash_bytes, stbds_hmget_key, stbds_hmget_key_ts, stbds_hmput_default, stbds_hmput_key, stbds_hmdel_key, stbds_shmode_func, stbds_hmfree_func, stbds_stralloc, stbds_strreset, strkey, str_dups`.\n\n## Behavioral verification (my own, not self-reported)\nI built the C library with CMake and wrote two C differential harnesses that re-declare the private ABI and the stb_ds macros exactly as the header does, then linked each harness against the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`:\n\n- **Main harness: 5944 lines of output, byte-identical** (`cmp` clean) — hash values for 16 strings × 7 seeds, `hash_bytes` over lengths 0–64 with high-bit/zero/0xff payloads, 1000-element array growth/pop/deln/delswap/setlen/setcap, 500-key int map with overwrite + interleaved deletes (exercising tombstone rebuild *and* shrink), struct-key maps, all three string-map modes (DEFAULT/STRDUP/ARENA), arena block growth + oversize path, `strkey` incl. `INT_MIN`, and `str_dups(0/1/2/37/1000/-5)`.\n- **Edge harness: 144 lines, byte-identical** — NULL/empty/table-less paths, `arrgrowf` capacity-doubling edges, non-zero `keyoffset` deletes, all 4 `shmode_func` modes, seed-walk determinism after `rand_seed`, 64-byte cache-line alignment of bucket storage, unaligned/long `hash_bytes`.\n- Also re-ran against a **C build with asserts enabled** (no `NDEBUG`): still identical, exit 0, so no assertion fires on any exercised path.\n\n## Bug-for-bug fidelity worth noting\n- **SipHash sign-extension quirk preserved**: `data = d[0]|...|(d[3]<<24)` is `int` arithmetic in C, so a high-bit byte makes the value negative and pollutes the upper 32 bits of the `size_t`. Reproduced via `i32 → i64 → u64`, including in the fall-through tail `switch` (`case 4`). The `hash_bytes_hi/ff` test vectors confirm this bit-for-bit.\n- `hash ^= hash ^ ROTR(hash,n)` (a no-op XOR pattern), the `hmput_key` inner \"limit\" loop that *omits* the `temp_key` update on match, `strkey`'s shared static buffer, and the `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", struct_by_value, value)` call in `str_dups` — where the 16-byte struct consumes two SysV integer vararg slots so `%d` reads the struct's `value`, not the third argument — all preserved (output `a <num>`, confirmed identical).\n\nImplementation uses `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"`, `#[repr(C)]` structs matching C layouts (32/16/24/128/104 bytes), the same libc allocator (`realloc`/`free`) and `printf`/`sprintf` for identical buffering, with wrapping arithmetic throughout. `c_src/` was not modified, and I removed all my scratch build/test directories."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":697,"cache_read_input_tokens":115343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":697,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"174bca25-3ee9-4374-ab59-9ab13495ffeb","uuid":"73ca6d0d-a5b4-488e-9a36-e3daf09e89e8","timestamp":"2026-08-27T17:41:53.569Z"}
